    "created_at": "2019-04-17T15:51:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-17T15:51:17Z",
    "body": "https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-fullscreen uses the fullscreen element directly. I suppose that exposing https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#fullscreen-element might allow other specs to set it, which would probably be difficult to do correctly, so we could expose a read-only notion for it.\r\n\r\n@annevk I wouldn't be particularly concerned about other specs trying to set the fullscreen element and just remove `data-noexport`. Would you do the same, or do you think a \"document is fullscreen\" notion would be better?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
